y"}]],["disgusting","/dɪsˈɡʌstɪŋ/","ADJ","ygrenç","отвратительный","extremely unpleasant","The soup smelled disgusting.","Çorbanyň ysy ygrenç boldy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":4,"lesson":"4B","page":40,"section":"vocabulary"}]],["irritated","/ˈɪrɪteɪtɪd/","ADJ","jynjygalan","раздражённый (слегка)","slightly annoyed","He got irritated by the questions.","Soraglardan jynjygalandy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","irritated by","New",[{"book":"int","unit":4,"lesson":"4B","page":40,"section":"vocabulary"}]],["thrilled","/θrɪld/","ADJ","şaý-sevinçli","в восторге","extremely happy and excited","She was thrilled with the result.","Netijeden şaý-sevinçli boldy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","thrilled with","New",[{"book":"int","unit":4,"lesson":"4B","page":40,"section":"vocabulary"},{"book":"advp","unit":5,"lesson":"5A","section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["puzzled","/ˈpʌzld/","ADJ","bulaşan (oýlanan)","озадаченный","unable to understand something","He looked puzzled by the question.","Soragdan bulaşan ýaly boldy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","puzzled by","New",[{"book":"int","unit":4,"lesson":"4B","page":40,"section":"vocabulary"}]],["beat","/biːt/","V","utmak","побеждать (соперника)","to win against a person or team","We beat the champions 2-1.","Çempionlary 2-1 utduk.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","beat a team","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5A","page":46,"section":"vocabulary_bank"},{"book":"adv","unit":9,"lesson":"9B","section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["league","/liːɡ/","N","liga","лига","a group of teams that play each other","Our team is top of the league.","Toparymyz liganyň başynda.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","the league table","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5A","page":46,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["referee","/ˌrefəˈriː/","N","emin","судья (в спорте)","the person who controls a game","The referee showed him a red card.","Emin oňa gyzyl kart görkezdi.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5A","page":46,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["spectator","/spekˈteɪtə(r)/","N","tomaşaçy","зритель","a person who watches a game","The stadium holds 40,000 spectators.","Stadion 40,000 tomaşaçy sygdyrýar.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5A","page":46,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["take up","/teɪk ʌp/","PHR","başlamak (sport)","начинать заниматься","to start a new sport or hobby","He took up swimming last year.","Geçen ýyl ýüzmä başlady.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","take up a sport","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5A","page":46,"section":"vocabulary_bank"},{"book":"upp","unit":4,"lesson":"4B","section":"vocabulary"},{"book":"intp","unit":7,"lesson":"7A","page":66,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["tennis court","/ˈtenɪs kɔːt/","N","tennis meýdançasy","теннисный корт","the area where you play tennis","The tennis court is free at six.","Tennis meýdançasy altyda boş.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","on court","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5A","page":46,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["pitch","/pɪtʃ/","N","oýun meýdany","футбольное поле","the field where football is played","The pitch was wet after the rain.","Ýagyşdan soň oýun meýdany öllüdi.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","football pitch","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5A","page":46,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["track","/træk/","N","ylgaýyş ýodasy","беговая дорожка","a path for running or racing","She ran two laps of the track.","Ýodanyň iki aýlawyny ylgady.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","running track","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5A","page":46,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["fan","/fæn/","N","janköýer","болельщик","a person who loves a team or star","He is a big fan of Arsenal.","Arsenalyň uly janköýeri.","A1","Oxford 3000","—","a big fan","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5A","page":46,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["circuit","/ˈsɜːkɪt/","N","trek, aýlawly ýol","трасса (авто/мото)","a track for motor races","The cars went round the circuit.","Ulaglar trek boýunça aýlandy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5A","page":46,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["hockey","/ˈhɒki/","N","hokkeý","хоккей","a team sport played with sticks and a ball or puck","He plays hockey at school.","Mekdepde hokkeý oýnaýar.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5A","page":46,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["warm up","/ˌwɔːm ˈʌp/","PHR","maşk etmek, gyzgynlyk","разминаться","to do gentle exercise before sport","Always warm up before a run.","Ylgamazdan öň hemişe maşk et.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5A","page":46,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["get injured","/ˌɡet ˈɪndʒəd/","PHR","şikes almak","получить травму","to hurt yourself doing sport","She got injured playing football.","Futbol oýnap şikes aldy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5A","page":46,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["stadium","/ˈsteɪdiəm/","N","stadion","стадион","a large place for sports with seats around it","The stadium holds 50,000 people.","Stadion 50,000 adam sygdyrýar.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5A","page":46,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["diving","/ˈdaɪvɪŋ/","N","suwa bökmek; daýwing","прыжки в воду; дайвинг","the sport of jumping into water, or swimming under water","She won a medal in diving.","Suwa bökmekde medal aldy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5A","page":46,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["work out","/ˌwɜːk ˈaʊt/","PHR","türgenleşmek","тренироваться","to do exercise to become strong and fit","I work out at the gym twice a week.","Hepdede iki gezek zalda türgenleşýärin.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5A","page":46,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["player","/ˈpleɪə/","N","oýunçy","игрок","a person who plays a sport or game","He is the best player in the team.","Toparda iň gowy oýunçy.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5A","page":46,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["sports hall","/ˈspɔːts hɔːl/","N","sport zaly","спортивный зал","a large indoor room for sport","We play basketball in the sports hall.","Sport zalynda basketbol oýnaýarys.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5A","page":46,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["slope","/sləʊp/","N","eňňit, gaýt","склон","a surface with one end higher than the other","He went down the ski slope.","Ol tizlenme gaýdyndan aşak düşdi.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5A","page":46,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["umpire","/ˈʌmpaɪə/","N","emin (tennis)","судья (в теннисе)","the person who makes sure players obey the rules in tennis","The umpire called the ball out.","Emin pökgini aut diýip yglan etdi.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5A","page":46,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["crowd","/kraʊd/","N","mähelle","толпа","a large group of people watching something","The crowd cheered loudly.","Mähelle gaty gygyrdy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5A","page":46,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["team","/tiːm/","N","topar","команда","a group of players in a sport","Which team do you support?","Haýsy topar goldaýarsyň?","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5A","page":46,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["captain","/ˈkæptɪn/","N","kapitan","капитан","the leader of a sports team","She is the captain of the volleyball team.","Woleýbol toparynyň kapitany.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5A","page":46,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["break up","/breɪk ʌp/","PHR","aýrylyşmak","расставаться","to end a relationship","They broke up after two years.","Iki ýyldan soň aýrylyşdylar.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","break up with","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5B","page":50,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["fall out","/fɔːl aʊt/","PHR","ara bozmak","ссориться","to stop being friendly after an argument","The sisters fell out over money.","Uýalar pul üstünde ara bozdy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","fall out with","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5B","page":50,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["go out with","/ɡəʊ aʊt wɪð/","PHR","duşuşmak","встречаться с","to spend time romantically with someone","She goes out with a musician.","Sazanda bilen duşuşýar.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","go out with someone","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5B","page":50,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["make up","/meɪk ʌp/","PHR","ara düzetmek","мириться","to become friendly again after a fight","They argued but soon made up.","Jedelleşdiler ýöne tiz ara düzetdiler.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","make up with","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5B","page":50,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["partner","/ˈpɑːtnə(r)/","N","ýoldaş","партнёр","the person you live or work with","Her partner cooks well.","Ýoldaşy gowy bişirýär.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","life partner","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5B","page":50,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["relationship","/rɪˈleɪʃnʃɪp/","N","gatnaşyk","отношения","the way two people feel about each other","They have a strong relationship.","Berk gatnaşyklary bar.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","close relationship","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5B","page":50,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["split up","/splɪt ʌp/","PHR","aýrylyşmak (jübüt)","расходиться","to end a relationship","The band split up in 2020.","Topar 2020-nji ýylda dargady.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","split up with","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5B","page":50,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["trust","/trʌst/","V","ynam etmek","доверять","to believe someone is honest","I trust her completely.","Oňa doly ynam edýärin.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","trust someone","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5B","page":50,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["lose touch","/ˌluːz ˈtʌtʃ/","PHR","aragatnaşygy ýitirmek","терять связь","to stop communicating with someone over time","We lost touch after school.","Mekdepden soň aragatnaşygy ýitirdik.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5B","page":50,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["get in touch","/ˌɡet ɪn ˈtʌtʃ/","PHR","habarlaşmak","связаться","to contact someone","She got in touch with me last year.","Geçen ýyl men bilen habarlaşdy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5B","page":50,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["get to know","/ˌɡet tə ˈnəʊ/","PHR","ýakyndan tanamak","узнавать (человека)","to spend time with someone and learn about them","We got to know each other at university.","Uniwersitetde birek-biregi ýakyndan tanadyk.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5B","page":50,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["propose","/prəˈpəʊz/","V","öýlenme teklibini etmek","делать предложение","to ask someone to marry you","He proposed on the beach.","Kenarda öýlenme teklip etdi.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5B","page":50,"section":"vocabulary_bank"},{"book":"intp","unit":9,"lesson":"9B","page":90,"section":"vocabulary"}]],["fancy","/ˈfænsi/","V","halamak, göwnünden turmak","нравиться (о человеке)","to be attracted to someone","I think she fancies him.","Onuň oňa göwni ýetýän bolsa gerek.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5B","page":50,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["ask out","/ˌɑːsk ˈaʊt/","PHR","duşuşyga çagyrmak","пригласить на свидание","to invite someone on a date","He finally asked her out.","Ahyry ony duşuşyga çagyrdy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5B","page":50,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["close friend","/ˌkləʊs ˈfrend/","N","ýakyn dost","близкий друг","a friend you know very well","She is one of my close friends.","Ýakyn dostlarymyň biri.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5B","page":50,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["flatmate","/ˈflætmeɪt/","N","öý ýoldaşy","сосед по квартире","a person you share a flat with","My flatmate cooks every evening.","Öý ýoldaşym her agşam nahar bişirýär.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":5,"lesson":"5B","page":50,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["audience","/ˈɔːdiəns/","N","tomaşaçylar","аудитория","the people watching a film or show","The audience clapped loudly.","Tomaşaçylar gaty el çarpdy.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","the whole audience","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6A","page":56,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["cast","/kɑːst/","N","aktýorlar düzümi","актёрский состав","all the actors in a film","The film has a brilliant cast.","Filmiň ajaýyp aktýorlar düzümi bar.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","the cast of","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6A","page":56,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["character","/ˈkærəktə(r)/","N","gahryman","персонаж","a person in a film or book","My favourite character is the doctor.","Iň söýýän gahrymanym lukman.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","the main character","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6A","page":56,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["ending","/ˈendɪŋ/","N","soňy","концовка","the last part of a story","The ending surprised everyone.","Soňy hemmäni geň galdyrdy.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","a happy ending","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6A","page":56,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["plot","/plɒt/","N","waka düzümi","сюжет","the story of a film or book","The plot was hard to follow.","Waka düzümini yzarlamak kyndy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","a complicated plot","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6A","page":56,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["scene","/siːn/","N","sahna (filmiň)","сцена","one part of a film","The final scene is unforgettable.","Soňky sahna ýatdan çykmaz.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","the opening scene","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6A","page":56,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["soundtrack","/ˈsaʊndtræk/","N","film saz toplumy","саундтрек","the music in a film","The soundtrack won an award.","Film saz toplumy baýrak aldy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","film soundtrack","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6A","page":56,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["special effects","/ˈspeʃl ɪˌfekts/","N","ýörite effektler","спецэффекты","images made by computers in films","The special effects look real.","Ýörite effektler hakyky görünýär.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","amazing special effects","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6A","page":56,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["star","/stɑː(r)/","N","ýyldyz (aktýor)","звезда","a famous actor","The star of the film is Turkish.","Filmiň ýyldyzy türk.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","film star","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6A","page":56,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["subtitle","/ˈsʌbtaɪtl/","N","titr","субтитры","words at the bottom of a film","I watched it with subtitles.","Titir bilen gördüm.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","with subtitles","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6A","page":56,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["villain","/ˈvɪlən/","N","ýaman gahryman","злодей","the bad person in a story","The villain steals the diamond.","Ýaman gahryman almazy ogarlaýar.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","the villain of","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6A","page":56,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["setting","/ˈsetɪŋ/","N","waka ýeri","место действия","where and when a story happens","The setting is 1920s Paris.","Waka ýeri 1920-nji ýyllaryň Pariži.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","the setting of","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6A","page":56,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["review","/rɪˈvjuː/","N","syn","рецензия","an article saying what a critic thinks","The film got good reviews.","Film gowy syn aldy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","write a review","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6A","page":56,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["based on","/beɪst ɒn/","PHR","esaslanýan","основанный на","using an earlier story or facts","The film is based on a true story.","Film hakyky wakadan esaslanýar.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","based on a novel","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6A","page":56,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["animation","/ˌænɪˈmeɪʃn/","N","animasiýa, multfilm","анимация","a film made with drawings or computer images","The children love this animation.","Çagalar bu multfilmi söýýär.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6A","page":56,"section":"vocabulary_bank"},{"book":"intp","unit":5,"lesson":"5A","page":46,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["historical film","/hɪˈstɒrɪkl fɪlm/","N","taryhy film","исторический фильм","a film set in the past","It is a historical film about the war.","Urug barada taryhy film.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6A","page":56,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["musical","/ˈmjuːzɪkl/","N","müzikl","мюзикл","a film where the actors sing and dance","We watched an old musical.","Köne müzikl gördük.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6A","page":56,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["thriller","/ˈθrɪlə/","N","triller","триллер","an exciting film, often about crime","The thriller kept us awake.","Triller bizi ukusyz saklady.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6A","page":56,"section":"vocabulary_bank"},{"book":"adv","unit":4,"lesson":"4A","section":"vocabulary"}]],["western","/ˈwestən/","N","western","вестерн","a film about the old American West","My grandfather loves westerns.","Atam westernleri söýýär.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6A","page":56,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["critic","/ˈkrɪtɪk/","N","tankytçy","критик","a person who writes opinions about films, books, etc.","The critics loved the film.","Tankytçylar filmi gowy gördi.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6A","page":56,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["extra","/ˈekstrə/","N","kömekçi aktýor","массовка, статист","a person employed to play a very small part in a film","He worked as an extra in a crowd scene.","Mähelle sahnaýynda kömekçi aktýor boldy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6A","page":56,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["script","/skrɪpt/","N","ssenariý","сценарий","the words of a film","The script was brilliant.","Ssenariý ajaýypdy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6A","page":56,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["sequel","/ˈsiːkwəl/","N","dowamy","продолжение, сиквел","a film that continues the story of an earlier film","The sequel was better than the first film.","Dowamy birinji filmden gowy boldy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6A","page":56,"section":"vocabulary_bank"},{"book":"adv","unit":4,"lesson":"4A","section":"vocabulary"}]],["set","/set/","N","surat düşürilýän meýdança","съемочная площадка","the place where a film is made","Visitors are not allowed on the set.","Myhmanlara meýdança rugsat berilmeýär.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6A","page":56,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["trailer","/ˈtreɪlə/","N","treýler","трейлер","short scenes from a film, shown to advertise it","I saw the trailer for the new Bond film.","Täze Bond filminiň treýlerini gördim.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6A","page":56,"section":"vocabulary_bank"},{"book":"adv","unit":4,"lesson":"4A","section":"vocabulary"}]],["dubbed","/dʌbd/","ADJ","dublyorlanan","дублированный","with the voices changed into another language","The film was dubbed into Russian.","Film rus diline dublyorlandy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6A","page":56,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["ankle","/ˈæŋkl/","N","ýanjyk","лодыжка","the joint between foot and leg","She twisted her ankle.","Ýanjygyny burady.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","twist your ankle","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["chest","/tʃest/","N","döş","грудь","the front part of the body above the stomach","He felt a pain in his chest.","Döşünde agyry duýdy.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","chest pain","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["elbow","/ˈelbəʊ/","N","tirsek","локоть","the middle joint of the arm","He rested his elbows on the table.","Tirselerini stola direledi.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["knee","/niː/","N","dyz","колено","the middle joint of the leg","The baby crawled on her knees.","Çaga dyzynyň üstünde emmekledi.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","on your knees","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["shoulder","/ˈʃəʊldə(r)/","N","egin","плечо","the part where the arm joins the body","She carried the bag on one shoulder.","Sumkany bir egninde göterdi.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["stomach","/ˈstʌmək/","N","garyn","живот","the part of the body where food goes","My stomach hurts.","Garynym agyrýar.","A1","Oxford 3000","—","stomach pain","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["thumb","/θʌm/","N","başam barmak","большой палец","the short thick finger on the hand","He cut his thumb.","Başam barmagyny kesdi.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["toe","/təʊ/","N","aya barmagy","палец ноги","one of the five parts at the end of the foot","I stubbed my toe on the bed.","Aýak barmagymy düşege kakdyrdym.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","stub your toe","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["waist","/weɪst/","N","bil","талия","the middle part of the body","The skirt was tight at the waist.","Ýubka bilinden gysyk bolady.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["wrist","/rɪst/","N","bil (el)","запястье","the joint between hand and arm","She wore a watch on her wrist.","Bilinde sagat bardy.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","break your wrist","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["muscle","/ˈmʌsl/","N","myşsa","мышца","tissue in the body that moves it","Exercise strengthens your muscles.","Maşk myşsalaryňy berkidýär.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","build muscle","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["skin","/skɪn/","N","deri","кожа","the covering of the body","Protect your skin from the sun.","Deriňi gün şöhlesinden gora.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","dry skin","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["calf","/kɑːf/","N","baldyr","икра","the back part of the lower leg","His calf ached after the run.","Ylgandan soň baldyry agyrdy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["forehead","/ˈfɔːhed/","N","maňlaý","лоб","the part of the face above the eyes","She wiped her forehead.","Maňlaýyny syldy.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["back","/bæk/","N","arka, bel","спина","the part of your body that you sit on","My back hurts after the journey.","Ýoldan soň arkam agyrýar.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["chin","/tʃɪn/","N","äň","подбородок","the part of your face under your mouth","He has a beard on his chin.","Äňinde sakgaly bar.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"},{"book":"upp","unit":7,"lesson":"7B","section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["ears","/ɪəz/","N","gulaklar","уши","the parts of your body you hear with","Rabbits have long ears.","Towşanlaryň gulaklary uzyn.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["eyes","/aɪz/","N","gözler","глаза","the parts of your body you see with","She has beautiful green eyes.","Owadan ýaşyl gözleri bar.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["face","/feɪs/","N","ýüz","лицо","the front part of your head","Wash your face every morning.","Her irden ýüzüňi ýuw.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["feet","/fiːt/","N","aýaklar","ступни","the parts of your body you stand on","My feet are tired.","Aýaklarym ýadaw.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["fingers","/ˈfɪŋɡəz/","N","barmaklar","пальцы (рук)","the five long parts of your hand","We have ten fingers.","On barmagymyz bar.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["hands","/hændz/","N","eller","кисти рук","the parts at the end of your arms","Clap your hands!","Elleriňi çarp!","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["head","/hed/","N","kelle","голова","the top part of your body with your brain","She nodded her head.","Kellesini atdy.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["legs","/leɡz/","N","aýaklar","ноги","the long parts of your body you walk with","Football players have strong legs.","Futbolçylaryň aýaklary güýçli.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["lips","/lɪps/","N","dodaklar","губы","the two soft parts of your mouth","Her lips were cold.","Dodaklary sowukdy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["mouth","/maʊθ/","N","agyz","рот","the part of your face you eat and speak with","Open your mouth and say \"ah\".","Agyzyňy aç we \"a\" diý.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["neck","/nek/","N","boýun","шея","the part between your head and your body","The giraffe has a long neck.","Zürafyň boýny uzyn.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["nose","/nəʊz/","N","burun","нос","the part of your face you smell with","He broke his nose playing rugby.","Regbi oýnap burnuny döwdi.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["tongue","/tʌŋ/","N","dil","язык","the part inside your mouth you taste with","You taste with your tongue.","Diliň bilen dadýarsyň.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"},{"book":"upp","unit":7,"lesson":"7B","section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["bite","/baɪt/","V","dişlemek","кусать","to use your teeth to cut something","The dog bit my hand.","It elimi dişledi.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["clap","/klæp/","V","el çarpmak","хлопать в ладоши","to hit your hands together to show you like something","The audience clapped loudly.","Tomaşaçylar gaty el çarpdy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["nod","/nɒd/","V","kelle atmak","кивать","to move your head down to say yes","She nodded and smiled.","Kelle atyp ýylgyrdy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["point","/pɔɪnt/","V","barmak bilen görkezmek","указывать","to show something with your finger","Don't point at people.","Adamlara barmak basma.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["smell","/smel/","V","ys almak","нюхать, пахнуть","to use your nose to find out about something","Smell the flowers!","Gülleri ysga!","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["smile","/smaɪl/","V","ýylgyrmak","улыбаться","to turn up the corners of your mouth","She smiled at the baby.","Çaga ýylgyrdy.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["stare","/steə/","V","tik seretmek","пристально смотреть","to look at someone for a long time","Don't stare at people.","Adamlara tik seretme.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"},{"book":"advp","unit":8,"lesson":"8B","section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["taste","/teɪst/","V","dat görmek","пробовать на вкус","to put food in your mouth to find out what it is like","Taste the soup and tell me if it needs salt.","Çorbany dat gör, duz gerekmi aýt.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["touch","/tʌtʃ/","V","ellemek","трогать","to put your hand on something","Do not touch the painting.","Suraty elleme.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["whistle","/ˈwɪsl/","V","şaşgy çalmak, huşlamak","свистеть","to make a high sound with your lips","The referee whistled.","Emin şaşgy çaldy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":6,"lesson":"6B","page":60,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["attend","/əˈtend/","V","gatnaşmak","посещать","to go to a school or event","She attended every lesson.","Her sapaga gatnaşdy.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","attend school","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7A","page":66,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["degree","/dɪˈɡriː/","N","diplom (ylmy dereje)","диплом, степень","a qualification from a university","He has a degree in physics.","Fizika boýunça diplomy bar.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","a degree in","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7A","page":66,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["graduate","/ˈɡrædʒueɪt/","V","gutarmak (uniwersitet)","оканчивать (вуз)","to finish university with a degree","She graduated last summer.","Geçen tomus uniwersiteti gutardy.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","graduate from","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7A","page":66,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["retake","/ˌriːˈteɪk/","V","täzeden tabşyrmak","пересдавать","to take an exam again","He had to retake the exam.","Synagy täzeden tabşyrmaly boldy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","retake an exam","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7A","page":66,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["skip","/skɪp/","V","geçirmek (sapagy)","пропускать","to not go to a lesson","Don't skip the first lesson.","Birinji sapagy geçirme.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","skip class","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7A","page":66,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["take an exam","/teɪk ən ɪɡˈzæm/","PHR","synag tabşyrmak","сдавать экзамен","to do an exam","They take an exam in June.","Iýunda synag tabşyrýarlar.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7A","page":66,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["lecturer","/ˈlektʃərə(r)/","N","mugallym (uniwersitet)","преподаватель","a teacher at a university","The lecturer explained it clearly.","Mugallym düşnükli düşündirdi.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7A","page":66,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["head teacher","/ˌhed ˈtiːtʃə(r)/","N","mekdep müdiri","директор школы","the leader of a school","The head teacher gave a speech.","Mekdep müdiri çykyş etdi.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7A","page":66,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["cheat","/tʃiːt/","V","aldamak (synagda)","списывать, жульничать","to break rules to gain an advantage","He was caught cheating in the test.","Synagda aldaýarka tutuldy.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","cheat in an exam","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7A","page":66,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["assignment","/əˈsaɪnmənt/","N","tabşyryk","задание","a piece of work for a course","The assignment is due Friday.","Tabşyryk anna güni tabşyrylmaly.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","finish an assignment","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7A","page":66,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["deadline","/ˈdedlaɪn/","N","möhlet","крайний срок","the last time you can finish something","The deadline is tomorrow.","Möhlet ertir.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","meet a deadline","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7A","page":66,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["campus","/ˈkæmpəs/","N","kampus","кампус","the grounds of a university","The campus has three libraries.","Kampusda üç kitaphana bar.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","on campus","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7A","page":66,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["misbehave","/ˌmɪsbɪˈheɪv/","V","özüňi erbet alyp barmak","плохо себя вести","to behave badly","If you misbehave, you will be punished.","Özüňi erbet alyp barsaň, jezalandyrylarsyň.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7A","page":66,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["state school","/ˌsteɪt ˈskuːl/","N","döwlet mekdebi","государственная школа","a school run by the government, usually free","Most children go to a state school.","Köp çaga döwlet mekdebe gatnaýar.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7A","page":66,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["private school","/ˌpraɪvət ˈskuːl/","N","hususy mekdep","частная школа","a school you have to pay to go to","Private schools can be very expensive.","Hususy mektepler gaty gymmat bolup biler.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7A","page":66,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["nursery school","/ˈnɜːsəri skuːl/","N","çagalar bagy","детский сад, ясли","a school for children between two and four","My daughter starts nursery school next month.","Gyzym indiki aý çagalar bagyna başlaýar.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7A","page":66,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["primary school","/ˈpraɪməri skuːl/","N","başlangyç mekdep","начальная школа","a school for children between five and eleven","He teaches at a primary school.","Başlangyç mekdepde sapak berýär.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7A","page":66,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["expelled","/ɪkˈspeld/","ADJ","mekdepden kowulan","исключённый (из школы)","made to leave school as a punishment","He was expelled for cheating.","Aldaw üçin mekdepden kowuldy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7A","page":66,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["punished","/ˈpʌnɪʃt/","ADJ","jezalandyrylan","наказанный","given a punishment for doing something wrong","She was punished for being late.","Giç galany üçin jezalandyryldy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7A","page":66,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["attic","/ˈætɪk/","N","ýerlik","чердак","the room under the roof","Old boxes are in the attic.","Köne gutular ýerlikde.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","in the attic","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7B","page":70,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["basement","/ˈbeɪsmənt/","N","zemin","подвал","the room below ground level","We store bikes in the basement.","Welosipedleri zeminde saklaýarys.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","in the basement","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7B","page":70,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["cottage","/ˈkɒtɪdʒ/","N","obadaky kiçi öý","коттедж, деревенский дом","a small house in the countryside","They rent a cottage by the lake.","Köliň ýanyndaky öýi kärendesine alýarlar.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7B","page":70,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["fence","/fens/","N","haýat","забор","a barrier round a garden","The cat jumped over the fence.","Pişik haýatdan bökdi.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","over the fence","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7B","page":70,"section":"vocabulary_bank"},{"book":"intp","unit":5,"lesson":"5B","page":50,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["ground floor","/ˈɡraʊnd flɔː(r)/","N","birinji gat","первый этаж (нижний)","the floor at street level","The shop is on the ground floor.","Dükan birinji gatda.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","on the ground floor","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7B","page":70,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["first floor","/ˌfɜːst ˈflɔː(r)/","N","ikinji gat","второй этаж (брит.)","the floor above the ground floor","Their flat is on the first floor.","Öýleri ikinji gatda.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","on the first floor","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7B","page":70,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["move in","/muːv ɪn/","PHR","göçüp gelmek","заселяться","to start living in a new home","They moved in last month.","Geçen aý göçüp geldiler.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","move in together","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7B","page":70,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["move out","/muːv aʊt/","PHR","göçüp gitmek","выселяться","to stop living in a home","He moved out at eighteen.","On sekiz ýaşynda göçüp gitdi.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","move out of","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7B","page":70,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["second floor","/ˌsekənd ˈflɔː/","N","ikinji gat","второй этаж","the floor above the first floor","They live on the second floor.","Ikinji gatda ýaşaýarlar.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7B","page":70,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["balcony","/ˈbælkəni/","N","balkon","балкон","a platform outside an upper window or door","We had breakfast on the balcony.","Balkonda ertirlik etdik.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7B","page":70,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["entrance","/ˈentrəns/","N","girelge","вход","the door or place where you go into a building","Wait for me at the main entrance.","Esasy girelgede garaş.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7B","page":70,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["roof","/ruːf/","N","üçek","крыша","the top part of a building","The cat sat on the roof.","Pişik üçekde otyrdy.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7B","page":70,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["chimney","/ˈtʃɪmni/","N","tüsseçe","дымоход, труба","a pipe on a roof that carries smoke away","Smoke came out of the chimney.","Tüsseçeden tüssa çykdy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7B","page":70,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["outskirts","/ˈaʊtskɜːts/","N","şäher etegi","окраина","the areas around the edge of a city","They live on the outskirts of town.","Şäher eteginde ýaşaýarlar.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7B","page":70,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["path","/pɑːθ/","N","ýodajyk","тропинка","a narrow way for walking","A stone path leads to the door.","Daş ýodajyk gapa alyp barýar.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7B","page":70,"section":"vocabulary_bank"},{"book":"intp","unit":5,"lesson":"5B","page":50,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["terrace","/ˈterəs/","N","terrassa; bitişik öýler hatary","терраса; ряд домов","an outdoor area next to a house, or a row of similar houses","We sat on the terrace in the sun.","Günde terrasa otyrдыk.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7B","page":70,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["top floor","/ˌtɒp ˈflɔː/","N","iň ýokarky gat","верхний этаж","the highest floor of a building","The flat is on the top floor.","Öý iň ýokarky gatda.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":7,"lesson":"7B","page":70,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["apply for","/əˈplaɪ fə(r)/","PHR","ýüz tutmak","подавать заявку","to formally ask for a job","She applied for three jobs.","Üç işe ýüz tutdy.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","apply for a job","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8A","page":76,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["colleague","/ˈkɒliːɡ/","N","işdeş","коллега","a person you work with","A colleague helped me with the report.","Işdeşim hasabatda kömek etdi.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8A","page":76,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["employee","/ɪmˈplɔɪiː/","N","işgär","работник","a person who works for a company","The company has 300 employees.","Kompaniýada 300 işgär bar.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8A","page":76,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["employer","/ɪmˈplɔɪə(r)/","N","iş beriji","работодатель","a person or company that gives jobs","Her employer pays for training.","Iş berijisi okuw üçin töleýär.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8A","page":76,"section":"vocabulary_bank"},{"book":"upp","unit":1,"lesson":"1A","section":"vocabulary"}]],["full-time","/ˌfʊl ˈtaɪm/","ADJ","doly ştatly","полный рабочий день","working all the usual hours","He found a full-time job.","Doly ştatly iş tapdy.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","full-time job","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8A","page":76,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["overtime","/ˈəʊvətaɪm/","N","goşmaça iş sagady","сверхурочные","extra hours worked","She did ten hours of overtime.","On sagat goşmaça işledi.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","do overtime","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8A","page":76,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["get a promotion","/ɡet ə prəˈməʊʃn/","PHR","wezipesi galmak","получить повышение","to move to a better job level","He got a promotion in March.","Mart aýynda wezipesi galdy.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8A","page":76,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["get the sack","/ɡet ðə sæk/","PHR","işden kowulmak","быть уволенным","to be dismissed from a job (informal)","He got the sack for being late.","Giç galany üçin işden kowuldy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8A","page":76,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["resign","/rɪˈzaɪn/","V","işden çekilmek","увольняться (самому)","to leave a job by choice","She resigned after five years.","Bäş ýyldan soň işden çekildi.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","resign from","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8A","page":76,"section":"vocabulary_bank"},{"book":"upp","unit":1,"lesson":"1A","section":"vocabulary"}]],["temporary","/ˈtemprəri/","ADJ","wagtlaýyn","временный","lasting for a limited time","It is only a temporary job.","Diňe wagtlaýyn iş.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","temporary work","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8A","page":76,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["permanent","/ˈpɜːmənənt/","ADJ","hemişelik","постоянный","lasting for ever; not temporary","She wants a permanent position.","Hemişelik wezipe isleýär.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","permanent job","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8A","page":76,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["workload","/ˈwɜːkləʊd/","N","iş ýüki","рабочая нагрузка","the amount of work you have","His workload doubled this month.","Iş ýüki şu aý iki esse artdy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","heavy workload","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8A","page":76,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["shift","/ʃɪft/","N","çalyşma","смена","a period of time worked","She works the night shift.","Gije çalyşmasynda işleýär.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","night shift","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8A","page":76,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["interview","/ˈɪntəvjuː/","N","söhbetdeşlik","собеседование","a meeting to decide if you get a job","The interview went well.","Söhbetdeşlik gowy geçdi.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","job interview","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8A","page":76,"section":"vocabulary_bank"},{"book":"upp","unit":1,"lesson":"1A","section":"vocabulary"},{"book":"intp","unit":4,"lesson":"4B","page":40,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["set up","/ˌset ˈʌp/","PHR","esaslandyrmak, gurmak","основывать (бизнес)","to start a business","She set up a business selling clothes online.","Onlaýn eşik satýan biznes esaslandyrdy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8A","page":76,"section":"vocabulary_bank"},{"book":"intp","unit":7,"lesson":"7A","page":66,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["be made redundant","/ˌmeɪd rɪˈdʌndənt/","PHR","işden boşadylmak","быть сокращённым","to lose your job because the company no longer needs you","He was made redundant last week.","Geçen hepde işden boşadyldy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8A","page":76,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["freelance","/ˈfriːlɑːns/","ADJ","frilans, erkin işleýän","фриланс, внештатный","working for different companies, not one employer","She is a freelance journalist.","Frilans žurnalist.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8A","page":76,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["part-time","/ˌpɑːt ˈtaɪm/","ADJ","ýarym ştatly","работающий неполный день","working only some hours of the week","He has a part-time job in a café.","Kafede ýarym ştatly işi bar.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8A","page":76,"section":"vocabulary_bank"},{"book":"upp","unit":1,"lesson":"1B","section":"vocabulary"}]],["self-employed","/ˌself ɪmˈplɔɪd/","ADJ","özi üçin işleýän","самозанятый","working for yourself, not for a company","He's self-employed now.","Häzir özi üçin işleýär.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8A","page":76,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["boss","/bɒs/","N","başlyk, boss","начальник, босс","the person who tells you what to do at work","Ask your boss for a holiday.","Bossuňdan dynç alyş sora.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8A","page":76,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["gardener","/ˈɡɑːdnə/","N","bagban","садовник","a person whose job is taking care of a garden","The gardener cut the grass.","Bagban ot ýazdy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8A","page":76,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["look for a job","/ˌlʊk fər ə ˈdʒɒb/","PHR","iş gözlemek","искать работу","to try to find work","She looked for a job online.","Onlaýn iş gözledi.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8A","page":76,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["quit","/kwɪt/","V","işi taşlamak","увольняться, бросать","to leave your job (American English)","He quit his job in June.","Iýunda işini taşlady.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8A","page":76,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["browse","/braʊz/","V","göz aýlamak","просматривать (магазины)","to look at things without planning to buy","I was just browsing, thanks.","Diňe göz aýlaýardym, sag boluň.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","browse the shelves","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8B","page":80,"section":"vocabulary"}]],["chain","/tʃeɪn/","N","dükanlar zynjyry","сеть магазинов","a group of shops with the same name","It is a big supermarket chain.","Uly marketler zynjyry.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","a chain store","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8B","page":80,"section":"vocabulary"}]],["goods","/ɡʊdz/","N","harytlar","товары","things that are sold","The goods arrived damaged.","Harytlar zeper ýetip geldi.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","electrical goods","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8B","page":80,"section":"vocabulary"}]],["in stock","/ɪn stɒk/","PHR","bar","в наличии","available to buy now","The blue one is in stock.","Gök reňklisi bar.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","have in stock","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8B","page":80,"section":"vocabulary"}]],["out of stock","/aʊt əv stɒk/","PHR","ýok","нет в наличии","not available to buy now","The phone is out of stock.","Telefon ýok.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","be out of stock","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8B","page":80,"section":"vocabulary"}]],["window shopping","/ˈwɪndəʊ ˌʃɒpɪŋ/","N","diňe seredip gezme","рассматривание витрин","looking at shops without buying","We did some window shopping.","Biraz diňe seredip gezdik.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8B","page":80,"section":"vocabulary"}]],["agreement","/əˈɡriːmənt/","N","ylalaşyk","соглашение","a decision people make together","We reached an agreement.","Ylalaşyga geldik.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","reach an agreement","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8B","page":80,"section":"vocabulary"},{"book":"adv","unit":10,"lesson":"10A","section":"wordbuilding"}]],["approval","/əˈpruːvl/","N","makullama","одобрение","the feeling that something is good","She nodded her approval.","Makullap baş atdy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","give approval","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8B","page":80,"section":"vocabulary"}]],["arrival","/əˈraɪvl/","N","gelmek","прибытие","the act of arriving","On arrival, go to reception.","Gelende resepsiýa baryň.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","on arrival","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8B","page":80,"section":"vocabulary"}]],["discovery","/dɪˈskʌvəri/","N","üsti açma","открытие (находка)","finding something new","It was an important discovery.","Möhüm üsti açma boldy.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","make a discovery","New",[{"book":"int","unit":8,"lesson":"8B","page":80,"section":"vocabulary"}]],["careless","/ˈkeələs/","ADJ","ünsüz","невнимательный","not taking care","A careless mistake cost us the game.","Ünsüz ýalňyşlyk oýny elimizden aldy.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":9,"lesson":"9A","page":86,"section":"vocabulary"},{"book":"intp","unit":1,"lesson":"1B","page":10,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["creative","/kriˈeɪtɪv/","ADJ","döredijilikli","творческий","good at thinking of new ideas","She found a creative solution.","Döredijilikli çözgüt tapdy.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","creative ideas","New",[{"book":"int","unit":9,"lesson":"9A","page":86,"section":"vocabulary"},{"book":"intp","unit":1,"lesson":"1B","page":10,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["deaf","/def/","ADJ","kereň","глухой","unable to hear","The deaf man read her lips.","Kereň adam onuň dodaklaryny okady.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":9,"lesson":"9A","page":86,"section":"vocabulary"}]],["economical","/ˌiːkəˈnɒmɪkl/","ADJ","tygşytly","экономичный","using little money or fuel","This car is very economical.","Bu maşyn gaty tygşytly.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":9,"lesson":"9A","page":86,"section":"vocabulary"}]],["effective","/ɪˈfektɪv/","ADJ","netijeli","эффективный","working well","The new system is more effective.","Täze ulgam has netijeli.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","an effective method","New",[{"book":"int","unit":9,"lesson":"9A","page":86,"section":"vocabulary"}]],["endless","/ˈendləs/","ADJ","tükeniksiz","бесконечный","seeming to have no end","The journey felt endless.","Syýahat tükeniksiz ýaly boldy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":9,"lesson":"9A","page":86,"section":"vocabulary"}]],["harmful","/ˈhɑːmfl/","ADJ","zyýanly","вредный","causing damage","Sugar is harmful to teeth.","Şeker dişlere zyýanly.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","harmful to","New",[{"book":"int","unit":9,"lesson":"9A","page":86,"section":"vocabulary"}]],["homeless","/ˈhəʊmləs/","ADJ","öýsüz","бездомный","having no home","They helped homeless people.","Öýsüz adamlara kömek etdiler.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":9,"lesson":"9A","page":86,"section":"vocabulary"}]],["hopeful","/ˈhəʊpfl/","ADJ","umytly","полный надежды","feeling that good things will happen","She felt hopeful about the result.","Netijeden umytly boldy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":9,"lesson":"9A","page":86,"section":"vocabulary"},{"book":"intp","unit":1,"lesson":"1B","page":10,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["ideal","/aɪˈdiːəl/","ADJ","ajaýyp (laýyk)","идеальный","perfect for a purpose","The weather was ideal for a picnic.","Howa piknik üçin ajaýyp boldy.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","ideal for","New",[{"book":"int","unit":9,"lesson":"9A","page":86,"section":"vocabulary"}]],["practical","/ˈpræktɪkl/","ADJ","amaly","практичный","useful and sensible","Wear practical shoes for the walk.","Ýöriş üçin amaly aýakgap geý.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","practical advice","New",[{"book":"int","unit":9,"lesson":"9A","page":86,"section":"vocabulary"}]],["predictable","/prɪˈdɪktəbl/","ADJ","öňünden aýdyp bolýan","предсказуемый","happening as you expect","The ending was completely predictable.","Soňy düýbünden öňünden aýdyp bolýan boldy.","B1","Oxford 5000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":9,"lesson":"9A","page":86,"section":"vocabulary"}]],["reasonable","/ˈriːznəbl/","ADJ","makul","разумный","fair and sensible","The price was reasonable.","Baha makul boldy.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","a reasonable price","New",[{"book":"int","unit":9,"lesson":"9A","page":86,"section":"vocabulary"}]],["suitable","/ˈsuːtəbl/","ADJ","laýyk","подходящий","right for a purpose","The film is not suitable for children.","Film çagalar üçin laýyk däl.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","suitable for","New",[{"book":"int","unit":9,"lesson":"9A","page":86,"section":"vocabulary"},{"book":"intp","unit":1,"lesson":"1B","page":10,"section":"vocabulary_bank"}]],["typical","/ˈtɪpɪkl/","ADJ","adaty","типичный","normal for its kind","A typical day starts at seven.","Adaty gün ýedide başlaýar.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","a typical example","New",[{"book":"int","unit":9,"lesson":"9A","page":86,"section":"vocabulary"}]],["unforgettable","/ˌʌnfəˈɡetəbl/","ADJ","ýatdan çykmaz","незабываемый","impossible to forget","We had an unforgettable holiday.","Ýatdan çykmaz dynç alyş geçirdik.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":9,"lesson":"9A","page":86,"section":"vocabulary"},{"book":"intp","unit":9,"lesson":"9A","page":86,"section":"wordbuilding"}]],["unnecessary","/ʌnˈnesəsəri/","ADJ","gereksiz","ненужный","not needed","The meeting was unnecessary.","Duşuşyk gereksiz boldy.","A2","Oxford 3000","—","—","New",[{"book":"int","unit":9,"lesson":"9A","page":86,"section":"vocabulary"}]],["unusual","/ʌnˈj